{"raw": {"https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5451649/assistant-professor-of-electrical-and-computer-engineering": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Electrical and Computer Engineering", "description": "Assistant Professor of Electrical and Computer Engineering Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Full Time Job Number 202600096 Division Kinsley School of Engineering, Sciences, & Technology Department Electrical & Computer Engineering & Computer Science Opening Date 08/18/2026 Closing Date 11/15/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Job Description: The Electrical and Computer Engineering program at York College of Pennsylvania invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor of Electrical and Computer Engineering beginning in either January or August 2027, with ongoing in-person teaching assignments in the fall and spring terms each year. Our ABET-accredited Electrical and Computer Engineering program has roughly 100 undergraduate students, five full-time faculty, and three supporting staff members. Our hands-on program is known for small class sizes and extensive student/faculty interaction. Students participate in design/build/test projects throughout the curriculum, culminating in a year-long Capstone Design project. Nearly all of our instruction occurs in versatile state-of-the-art lecture/laboratory spaces. Our two-semester co-operative education requirement is a key component of our overall academic program, and is a substantive expression of our focus on pragmatic applications of concepts and skills embedded throughout our curriculum. Essential Functions For this position, we seek candidates that are eager to teach undergraduates in a student-centered, project-based learning environment. Applicants with a desire to utilize their knowledge and skills in mentoring undergraduates, conducting research with undergraduates, and teaching introductory electrical and computer engineering courses should apply. The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate electrical and computer engineering related courses, including computer architecture, analog circuits, microprocessor and embedded systems, signal processing, and robotics. Other responsibilities may include advising students on independent study and capstone design projects, as well as teaching special topics in an area of expertise. The successful candidate will be active in curriculum and laboratory development and scholarly research. Experience and Education Required An earned Ph.D. in Computer or Electrical Engineering or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment is required. ABD will be considered. Required Skills and Qualifications Candidates are expected to demonstrate the potential for outstanding teaching and advising, ongoing college service, professional development, developing undergraduate courses, and working with industry and undergraduate students in applied research. Further qualifications include the interest and ability to teach a wide range of undergraduate engineering courses. Top candidates will demonstrate the potential for outstanding teaching and mentoring of undergraduates, and those candidates with teaching or industry experience are highly valued. Strong communication skills, the ability to work with undergraduate students, and ability to teach in a project-based setting are essential. Those candidates with research interests in embedded systems, robotics and autonomous systems, and machine learning or artificial intelligence are preferred. Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . We offer a complete benefits package to full-time employees that includes, but is not limited to: health care, dental, vision, retirement, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long-term disability, holidays, vacation, sick leave, tuition remission and tuition discount programs. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you possess, or will you have by the start of the appointment, an earned Doctorate in Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a closely related field? Yes No 02 Do you have interest in teaching a broad range of undergraduate engineering courses? Yes No 03 Do you have the ability to work effectively in a collegiate setting with students, faculty, administrators, and staff? Yes No 04 Do you have research interest in embedded systems, robotics, and autonomous systems, machine learning or artificial intelligence? Yes No 05 Do you have teaching experience? Yes No 06 Do you have industry experience? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5501600/assistant-professor-of-graphic-design": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Graphic Design", "description": "Assistant Professor of Graphic Design Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Full Time Job Number 202600111 Division School of the Arts, Humanities, Education, and Social Sciences Department Department of the Visual and Performing Arts Opening Date 10/01/2026 Closing Date 11/16/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Job Description: The Department of Visual and Performing Arts at York College of Pennsylvania invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Graphic Design in the Bachelor of Fine Arts (BFA) degree program beginning in August 2027. We seek an engaged educator and active practitioner with dedicated expertise in User Experience/User Interface Design and Motion Graphics. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in advancing our curriculum in interactive media, delivering high-impact studio instruction, and contributing to the academic and professional development of our undergraduate students. York College of Pennsylvania (YCP) thrives on cross-disciplinary collaboration, active creative practices, and faculty mentorship. We are a tight-knit community where your voice shapes the curriculum, your active studio practice is celebrated, and our gallery system and industry-standard studios provide a vibrant canvas for both you and YCP students. Located near major creative and cultural centers throughout the Mid-Atlantic region (Baltimore, New York City, Philadelphia, and Washington, D.C.), we are situated in a region with thriving creative entrepreneurship opportunities and community-engaged art. YCP can offer the perfect launchpad to connect your students with major cultural hubs while thriving in a supportive, collaborative peer environment. Additionally, the York art community provides opportunities for professional networking, internships, industry partnerships, and community engagement. York City's vibrant arts community further supports creative entrepreneurship, experiential learning, and partnerships that connect students with contemporary design practice. Outcome: The successful candidate will teach an engaging mix of foundational and advanced BFA courses, spanning from typography, identity systems, design research, and professional practice to UX/UI, and motion graphics with the opportunity to modernize and expand program offerings to reflect emerging trends in interactive media, emerging technologies, and contemporary design practice. Beyond cultivating student excellence in the studio environment, the successful candidate will provide dedicated mentorship through academic advising, engage in service to our academic community, and maintain a robust, active creative or scholarly practice supported by the institution. Essential Functions Teach four 3-credit courses per semester (Fall and Spring) Provide mentorship to students via academic advising Service to the college community Maintain an active scholarly and/or creative practice Experience and Education Required We are looking for a collaborative colleague who can bring a healthy mixture of classroom experience and real-world insight. Required: Terminal degree in Graphic Design, Interactive Media, Visual Communication, or a closely related field (MFA or equivalent). Demonstrated expertise in UX/UI Design and Motion Graphics software/workflows. Evidence of an active, high-level professional practice or scholarly record. A clear commitment to undergraduate teaching excellence and student mentorship with a minimum of two years of college-level teaching practice. Preferred: Minimum of three years of professional experience in the graphic design industry. Experience with cross-disciplinary collaboration or community-partnered design projects. Knowledge of emerging design technologies, including evolving AI-assisted workflows, accessibility standards, and creative entrepreneurship. Required Skills and Qualifications Additional Required Skills and Qualifications: Excellent communication skills and commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration. Ability to supervise and motivate undergraduate students. To ensure full consideration, please submit the following materials electronically: 1. Cover letter detailing your teaching philosophy and professional practice 2. Curriculum Vitae (CV) 3. Link to digital portfolio of professional work 4. Link to portfolio of student work from courses taught 5. Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts 6. Contact information for three confidential letters of recommendation Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . We offer a complete benefits package to full-time employees that includes, but is not limited to: health care, dental, vision, retirement, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long-term disability, holidays, vacation, sick leave, tuition remission and tuition discount programs. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you have a Terminal Degree in Graphic Design or a related field? Yes No 02 Do you have experience teaching in higher education? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5496059/assistant-associate-or-professor-of-biomedical-engineering": {"title": "Assistant, Associate or Professor of Biomedical Engineering", "description": "Assistant, Associate or Professor of Biomedical Engineering Location York, PA Job Type Faculty, Full Time Job Number 202600107 Division Kinsley School of Engineering, Sciences, & Technology Department Civil & Mechanical Engineering Opening Date 09/25/2026 Closing Date 12/1/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Questions Position Summary The Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering program at York College of Pennsylvania invites applications for a tenure-track (open rank) Professor of Biomedical Engineering position beginning in the Fall 2027 semester, coinciding with the arrival of the first class of students for our new Biomedical Engineering program. The overall department houses approximately 300 undergraduates, eleven full-time faculty members, and five part-time and full-time staff members. The ABET-accredited programs in our department are characterized as hands-on with small class sizes and extensive student/faculty interactions. Students in the engineering departments participate in design/build/test projects throughout the curriculum, culminating with a yearlong Capstone Design project that requires a functioning prototype. This includes several courses in our state-of-the-art Materials Science and Fluid Mechanics laboratories. A keystone of the York College engineering programs is that our students participate in two semesters of engineering work in an industry setting as part of our required co-operative learning program prior to graduation. This gives our students valuable experience that they can then apply in their classroom learning. For this position, we seek candidates that are eager to teach undergraduates in a student-centered, project-based learning environment. Applicants with a desire to utilize their knowledge and skills in mentoring undergraduates, conducting research with undergraduates, and teaching introductory engineering courses should apply. Expertise across all areas of biomedical engineering is valued, however, knowledge of quantitative physiology and bioinstrumentation are especially valued. The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate foundational and biomedical engineering courses throughout the fall and spring semesters. Additionally, the successful candidate will be expected to advise undergraduate students regarding their course curriculum and on career matters; perform service to the department, college, and/or community; and show the potential for research work that can involve undergraduate students. The successful candidate will also help develop and refine the courses within the new Biomedical Engineering program. Experience and Education Required Applicants must have an Ph.D. in Biomedical Engineering or Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field by the start date of the appointment. Required Skills and Qualifications Further qualifications include the interest and ability to teach undergraduate engineering courses in the area of bioinstrumentation and quantitative physiology. Top candidates will demonstrate the potential for outstanding teaching, and those candidates with prior teaching experience are highly valued. Strong communication skills, the ability to work with undergraduate students, and ability to teach in a project-based setting are essential. Additional Information York College of Pennsylvania is an Equal Opportunity Employer and Non-Discriminatory . For a copy of York College's Annual Security Report, you may contact the Office of Campus Safety or visit the website: Annual Security Report . We offer a complete benefits package to full-time employees that includes, but is not limited to: health care, dental, vision, retirement, flexible spending accounts, life insurance, long-term disability, holidays, vacation, sick leave, tuition remission and tuition discount programs. To learn more details, visit our benefits page . 01 Do you have an earned Doctorate in Biomedical Engineering or a related field? Yes No 02 Do you have experience teaching in higher education? Yes No 03 Do you have non-academic work experience related to biomedical engineering, mechanical engineering, or a related field? Yes No Required Question Employer York College of Pennsylvania Address 441 Country Club Road York, Pennsylvania, 17403 Phone 717-815-1320 Website https://www.ycp.edu/ Apply"}}, "rows": {"https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5451649/assistant-professor-of-electrical-and-computer-engineering": {"school_id": 1228, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5451649/assistant-professor-of-electrical-and-computer-engineering", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor of Electrical and Computer Engineering", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Electrical and Computer Engineering; artificial intelligence; autonomous systems", "deadline_of_application": "11/15/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5501600/assistant-professor-of-graphic-design": {"school_id": 1228, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5501600/assistant-professor-of-graphic-design", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor of Graphic Design", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Visual and Performing Arts", "area_key_words": "Graphic Design", "deadline_of_application": "11/16/2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5496059/assistant-associate-or-professor-of-biomedical-engineering": {"school_id": 1228, "posting_url": "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ycp/faculty/jobs/5496059/assistant-associate-or-professor-of-biomedical-engineering", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant, Associate or Professor of Biomedical Engineering", "position_type": "Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering program", "area_key_words": "Biomedical Engineering; bioinstrumentation", "deadline_of_application": "12/1/2026", "position_start_date": ""}}, "school_id": 1228, "status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-10-21T00:02:30+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-21T00:02:30+00:00", "last_error": ""}